          "text": "Clinical Indication:  \nEvaluation of focal seizures with impaired awareness, with onset at age 34 and an estimated frequency of approximately 3 events per year. The reported etiology is genetic, associated with a DEPDC5 c.4396C>T variant. Seizures are reported as drug-responsive. Current antiseizure medications are topiramate and valproate.\n\nTechnique:  \nRoutine EEG using standard scalp electrodes placed according to the international 10–20 system. The supplied record contains no EEG waveform data for review.\n\nFindings:  \nBackground activity, state changes, interictal epileptiform discharges, and ictal patterns cannot be assessed because EEG waveform data are not available.\n\nImpression:  \nNo electroencephalographic interpretation can be made from the supplied clinical information alone.",
